WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
You couldn't avoid Piața
Matache. You were tied to it.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.300
It was a whole world.

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.400
You met people.

4
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:12.600
Sooner or later, you inevitably
got attached to certain people

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.600
you knew you could count on.

6
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.000
They'd pick things out for you,
or sometimes keep them aside,

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.000
if they were things that
were hard to come by.

8
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:30.200
They'd tell you: "I'm not in
tomorrow... or I am, I don't know,

9
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.500
but I'll put some aside for you."

10
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:40.800
And then there was another place you
couldn't avoid: the market hall.

11
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:46.200
The hall of Matache the Butcher –

12
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:52.000
which is actually where
it all comes from:

13
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Matache, the Matache area,
comes from this butcher.

14
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:00.000
And his market hall.

15
00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:07.500
I remember there were
different times – good times,

16
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:15.500
when you could find produce,
food and everything you needed.

17
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:23.400
And then, from the '80s on,
came a very, very bad time.

18
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:28.400
Even so, it was still a
place where some

19
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.200
meat and fish still came
in... but the queues were

20
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.900
hellish. Absolutely.

21
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.600
And it was freezing... the wind
blew right through the hall.

22
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:49.100
I used to watch those men
cutting up the carcasses,

23
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:57.300
the frozen fish, the noise of the
fish crates as they tipped them out.

24
00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.300
But you were glad just
to find something.
